  {
   "id": 631729,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><span>In this scatter plot, which sentence best describes how the two variables are related?</span></p>\n<p><strong> <img alt=\"SCATTER PLOT THAT CAN BE APPROXIMATED BY A LINE, WHERE THE \\(y\\)-values INCREASE AS THE \\(x\\)-values INCREASE\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"327\" src=\"exercises/media/67cb0f41fdbe2373.jpg\" width=\"350\"> </strong></p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222526,
     "content_html": "As hot dog prices go up, soft drink prices go down."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222527,
     "content_html": "At different locations, as hot dog prices increase, small soda prices also increase."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222525,
     "content_html": "Hot dog prices and small soft drink prices are not related."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222524,
     "content_html": "The more hot dogs that are bought, the more sodas that are bought."
    }
   ],
